WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.248
Theo drafts a postcard for AMG’s health clients.

00:00:03.248 --> 00:00:07.308
Maryland law and MIA rules require every advertisement to be

00:00:07.308 --> 00:00:10.961
truthful and not misleading in fact or by implication.

00:00:10.961 --> 00:00:15.833
The ad must identify the insurer, describe benefits accurately, and disclose limitations,

00:00:15.833 --> 00:00:20.299
exclusions and waiting periods with the same prominence as the benefits.

00:00:20.299 --> 00:00:24.765
It may not imply that a limited policy is comprehensive, exaggerate

00:00:24.765 --> 00:00:29.231
the ease of claims, or use testimonials that are not genuine.

00:00:29.231 --> 00:00:34.508
The insurer is responsible for every advertisement used on its behalf, including the

00:00:34.508 --> 00:00:39.380
producer’s own, which is why carriers require advance approval of producer materials.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.418
Some claims are banned outright.

00:00:41.418 --> 00:00:46.308
An advertisement may not suggest that a policy is approved, endorsed or

00:00:46.308 --> 00:00:51.198
offered by a government agency, or use words such as Medicare or

00:00:51.198 --> 00:00:55.273
Social Security in a way that implies a government connection.

00:00:55.273 --> 00:01:00.570
It may not describe coverage as guaranteed issue when underwriting applies, or state

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:05.868
that no medical questions will be asked when the application contains health questions.

00:01:05.868 --> 00:01:09.535
It may not misrepresent dividends, cash values or renewability.

00:01:09.535 --> 00:01:14.833
In Maryland, false advertising and misrepresentation are unfair trade practices that carry fines,

00:01:14.833 --> 00:01:20.130
restitution and license discipline, whether the author is the insurer or the producer.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:25.649
If a member insurer becomes insolvent, the Maryland Life and Health Insurance

00:01:25.649 --> 00:01:31.168
Guaranty Corporation continues coverage and pays claims for Maryland residents, within limits.

00:01:31.168 --> 00:01:36.227
Coverage of health benefit plans, meaning major medical and basic hospital,

00:01:36.227 --> 00:01:40.826
medical and surgical coverage, is protected up to 500,000 dollars.

00:01:40.826 --> 00:01:45.885
Disability income and long-term care are each protected up to 300,000

00:01:45.885 --> 00:01:50.943
dollars, life insurance death benefits up to 300,000 dollars, cash values

00:01:50.943 --> 00:01:55.542
up to 100,000 dollars and annuities up to 250,000 dollars.

00:01:55.542 --> 00:01:59.222
Every authorized insurer and HMO must be a

00:01:59.222 --> 00:02:02.901
member and is assessed to fund the payments.

00:02:02.901 --> 00:02:07.040
Self-funded employer plans and nonadmitted insurers are not covered.

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:09.920
The corporation exists to protect policyholders after a failure,

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:12.480
not to make a weak insurer look safe.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:16.000
Maryland law prohibits any person from using the existence of the

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.200
guaranty corporation in the sale, solicitation or advertising of insurance.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.720
Theo may not say that a policy is backed by the

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.240
state or that the client cannot lose because of the corporation.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:30.720
The insurer delivers a required summary notice about the corporation with the policy, and

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:34.880
that notice itself states that the corporation may not be used in sales.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:38.400
Using the safety net as an inducement is grounds for discipline.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:42.124
In Rosa’s kitchen, Theo presents a disability income policy.

00:02:42.124 --> 00:02:46.677
He identifies himself as a licensed producer and names the insurer.

00:02:46.677 --> 00:02:49.987
He explains the benefit amount, the elimination period

00:02:49.987 --> 00:02:53.298
and the benefit period before he mentions price.

00:02:53.298 --> 00:02:57.022
He states the exclusions, the pre-existing condition rule and

00:02:57.022 --> 00:03:00.333
whether the policy is noncancelable or guaranteed renewable.

00:03:00.333 --> 00:03:03.644
He compares policies only on accurate, complete terms

00:03:03.644 --> 00:03:06.954
and never disparages another insurer with false statements.

00:03:06.954 --> 00:03:11.506
He leaves an outline of coverage that summarizes benefits and limits.

00:03:11.506 --> 00:03:17.300
A fair presentation lets the buyer decide with the same facts the producer has.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:20.685
Selling health insurance is persuasion built on accurate facts.

00:03:20.685 --> 00:03:25.576
Crossing the line means persuading with facts that are false, incomplete or implied.

00:03:25.576 --> 00:03:30.842
Omitting the elimination period, calling a hospital indemnity policy health insurance, hinting at government

00:03:30.842 --> 00:03:36.108
backing, or using the guaranty corporation to reassure a nervous buyer each crosses it.

00:03:36.108 --> 00:03:41.374
Maryland treats these as unfair trade practices with penalties that reach the producer personally.

00:03:41.374 --> 00:03:45.888
Later lessons on unfair trade practices and discipline return to these rules;

00:03:45.888 --> 00:03:50.402
this lesson gives you the standard: say what the policy does, say

00:03:50.402 --> 00:03:54.540
what it does not, and say who stands behind it truthfully.
